   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency distribution of animal feeds to the most vulnerable producers in Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will serve for mitigating the social and economic impact of COVID-19 pandemic, specifically targeting smallholding poultry and dairy farmers who were severely affected by drastic increase of feed price. The increasing prices of inputs might lead small-scale poultry and dairy cow producers to abandon the production, which would negatively affect the nutritional status of household members in short term, and unavailability of animal source foods in the markets in the longer term. To sustain food production in the coming production seasons is essential to minimize both of the short and long-term negative impact of the complex crisis to food security in Syria.</narrative>
  </description>
